    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on the owner read model so it is `true` when any of the three risk signals hold, and `false` otherwise. Each piece of logic lives in its natural home:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `riskFlag` read-only boolean to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec), documenting the three conditions.\n\n2. **`DisposableEmailRule`** (`rest/validation`) \u2014 This class already owns all disposable-email knowledge, so I added `isDisposableAdjacent(email)` there. It reuses the existing blocklist by deriving each blocked provider's second-level label (e.g. `mailinator`) once, and flags any email whose domain shares such a label \u2014 catching the same provider under a different TLD (`mailinator.net`) or as a subdomain (`mx.mailinator.com`) without being on the exact blocklist (exact disposables are already rejected at creation by `@NotDisposableEmail`). I also refactored the shared `@`-domain extraction into a `domainOf` helper so `isDisposable` and `isDisposableAdjacent` don't duplicate it.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 Added a small `resolveRiskFlag(owner)` derivation alongside the other derived read-only fields (`ownerSegment`, `contactPreference`, etc.), wired via `@Mapping`. It ORs the three signals, each already exposed by the owner or the rule:\n   - possible duplicate \u2192 `owner.isPossibleDuplicate()`\n   - disposable-adjacent email \u2192 `DisposableEmailRule.isDisposableAdjacent(owner.getEmail())`\n   - city over soft capacity \u2192 `owner.isCapacityWarning()` (the persisted 40\u201349 \"approaching the 50 cap\" snapshot, i.e. over the soft-capacity warning threshold)\n\nI placed the aggregation in the mapper rather than the `Owner` entity to avoid a model\u2192`rest.validation` layering dependency \u2014 the mapper already legitimately depends on the `rest.validation` resolvers and is where all the other derived read-only DTO fields are assembled.\n\nOne interpretation note: I mapped \"over its soft capacity\" to the owner's persisted `capacityWarning` (a creation-time snapshot), consistent with how `possibleDuplicate` is also a persisted signal. This keeps the mapper free of a repository dependency. If the intent was instead to reflect the city's *current* occupancy on each read, that would require threading the `ClinicService` into the read path \u2014 let me know and I can adjust.",
